1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,008
This is the Wall of ScrappyT.

2
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:03,855
Its signature Cent,

3
00:00:03,947 --> 00:00:08,196
number 7139, was struck in 1967,

4
00:00:08,522 --> 00:00:12,410
carries a full desert patina, and is a Ghost Cent.

5
00:00:13,362 --> 00:00:15,603
Ghost means a full or near-full

6
00:00:15,662 --> 00:00:18,390
patina sets Lincoln apart from the field.

7
00:00:19,202 --> 00:00:21,175
Of the thirty-three Ghost Cents,

8
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:24,298
only thirteen carry a full desert patina.

9
00:00:25,111 --> 00:00:27,480
The Wall holds 41 Cents in two

10
00:00:27,538 --> 00:00:31,405
wallets, from 1956 to 1982,

11
00:00:31,914 --> 00:00:33,679
which puts it in the Quarter Club,

12
00:00:34,121 --> 00:00:36,722
for twenty-five to forty-nine Cents.

13
00:00:37,325 --> 00:00:39,206
One of them is a wheat penny,

14
00:00:39,646 --> 00:00:41,957
minted 1958 or earlier,

15
00:00:42,201 --> 00:00:44,152
with two ears of wheat on the back.

16
00:00:44,756 --> 00:00:48,807
It is from 1956, the earliest year on the Wall.

17
00:00:49,411 --> 00:00:52,500
It holds three Cents from 1971,

18
00:00:52,825 --> 00:00:54,716
for the 1971 Club.

19
00:00:55,482 --> 00:00:57,771
Two of its Cents carry a full patina:

20
00:00:58,130 --> 00:01:00,347
the full desert and a full red.

21
00:01:00,997 --> 00:01:02,518
Two are Iridescent,

22
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,260
a copper surface overlaid

23
00:01:04,307 --> 00:01:06,570
with gold, violet and blue.

24
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:08,984
And two are Ghost Cents.

25
00:01:09,751 --> 00:01:11,772
The Wall completes six Sets.

26
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:13,501
A Spectrum Set:

27
00:01:13,837 --> 00:01:15,358
a significant verdigris,

28
00:01:15,498 --> 00:01:16,799
a significant obsidian,

29
00:01:17,194 --> 00:01:19,423
a full red, a full desert,

30
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:21,745
a notable gold and an orange.

31
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:24,787
Notable means clearly visible but local,

32
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:27,712
significant a major presence on the face,

33
00:01:27,956 --> 00:01:30,766
and full means the patina dominates the coin.

34
00:01:31,718 --> 00:01:35,596
As of October 2026, ScrappyT is one of only

35
00:01:35,665 --> 00:01:38,242
fifteen collectors to hold a Spectrum Set.

36
00:01:38,939 --> 00:01:40,159
A Chronicle Set:

37
00:01:40,855 --> 00:01:46,962
a Cent from 1971, from 1979 and from 1982.

38
00:01:47,739 --> 00:01:48,900
A Full Mint Set:

39
00:01:49,388 --> 00:01:53,162
an S mint, a D mint and a Cent with no mint mark.

40
00:01:53,927 --> 00:01:55,472
A Contamination Set,

41
00:01:55,891 --> 00:01:57,352
four of the twelve contamination

42
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,629
types: special oddities,

43
00:01:59,733 --> 00:02:03,507
obscure adhesive, speckles and alien secretion.

44
00:02:04,168 --> 00:02:05,816
And a 1970s Set

45
00:02:06,141 --> 00:02:07,802
and a 1980s Set:

46
00:02:08,406 --> 00:02:12,271
every mint year from 1970 to 1982.

47
00:02:13,223 --> 00:02:15,175
The Wall carries Diamond Hands:

48
00:02:15,419 --> 00:02:17,194
it has held its position for at least

49
00:02:17,252 --> 00:02:19,586
a year, with little to no selling.

50
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,872
And it is a Mint Keeper: ScrappyT

51
00:02:23,046 --> 00:02:24,556
minted four of its Cents

52
00:02:24,881 --> 00:02:27,307
and still holds them, never sold.

53
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,804
Find all of the Collector Walls

54
00:02:29,872 --> 00:02:32,555
on cents.vision under Collectors.
